That's it: edit NETHACK.CNF so that levels are no longer stored in ram:,
but stored on floppy or hard disk. I played all versions of Amiga nethack
on a 1 meg 1000 for years and had no problems. 
 
Make sure you are running 3.0j - other versions of nethack, especially those
with the pretty color graphic monsters and dungeons, are not so stable. 3.0j
never crashed once on me.

